 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Motivation">Motivation</h1>
    <p>As part of the effort to make Airflow AI-native, this AIP introduces=
 a pluggable extension point for retry decisions. The core abstraction (<co=
de>RetryPolicy</code>) is provider-agnostic and useful on its own for decla=
rative exception handling. The <code>LLMRetryPolicy</code> in the Common AI=
 provider builds on this to bring intelligent, LLM-powered error classifica=
tion to any Airflow task, a concrete example of how AI capabilities integra=
te into Airflow's existing task lifecycle rather than requiring new operato=
rs or wrappers.</p>
    <p>Airflow's retry mechanism applies uniform behavior regardless of err=
or type. When a task fails, the system retries based on a static count (<co=
de>retries</code>) and delay (<code>retry_delay</code>) with no awareness o=
f <em>what</em> went wrong. This creates three recurring problems:</p>
    <ol>
     <li><strong>Wasted retries on permanent failures.</strong> Authenticat=
ion errors, schema validation errors, and permission denials are retried th=
e same number of times as transient network issues. Each retry is guarantee=
d to fail, wasting compute, delaying DAG completion, and cluttering logs.</=
li>
     <li><strong>Suboptimal timing for rate-limited APIs.</strong> When a t=
ask hits a rate limit with a "retry after 60 seconds" header, Airflow eithe=
r retries too early (triggering the same 429) or too late (using the defaul=
t 5-minute delay when 60 seconds would suffice). There is no mechanism to a=
dapt the retry delay to the error.</li>
     <li><strong>No separation between retry logic and task logic.</strong>=
 Users who want error-aware retries must wrap their task code in try/except=
 blocks, manually raise <code>AirflowFailException</code> for non-retryable=
 errors, and sleep for custom durations. This mixes retry policy with busin=
ess logic and is not reusable across tasks.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Currentworkaroundsandtheirlimit=
ations">Current workarounds and their limitations</h2>
    <p>Today, users have three options:</p>
    <ul>
     <li><strong>AirflowFailException</strong>: Raise it inside a task to p=
revent retries. This works but requires modifying every task's code and doe=
sn't allow custom delays.</li>
     <li><strong>on_retry_callback</strong>: Called on retry, but cannot pr=
event the retry or change the delay. It's fire-and-forget.</li>
     <li><strong>External provider</strong>: The <a class=3D"external-link"=
 href=3D"https://github.com/ertancelik/airflow-provider-smart-retry" rel=3D=
"nofollow">airflow-provider-smart-retry</a> wraps tasks in an <code>LLMSmar=
tRetryOperator</code>. This requires replacing the task's operator, couples=
 retry logic to a specific LLM backend (Ollama), and breaks the standard DA=
G authoring experience.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>None of these approaches provide a clean, reusable way to configure =
per-exception retry behavior as a parameter on any task.</p>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Quickstart">Quick start</h2>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">from airflow.sdk.definitions.retry_policy import=
 ExceptionRetryPolicy, RetryRule, RetryAction
from datetime import timedelta

@task(
    retries=3D5,
    retry_policy=3DExceptionRetryPolicy(rules=3D[
        RetryRule(exception=3D"requests.exceptions.HTTPError", action=3DRet=
ryAction.RETRY,
                  retry_delay=3Dtimedelta(minutes=3D5), reason=3D"Rate limi=
t"),
        RetryRule(exception=3D"google.auth.exceptions.RefreshError", action=
=3DRetryAction.FAIL,
                  reason=3D"Auth failure, not retryable"),
    ]),
)
def call_api():
    ...

# For AI-based retries
llm_policy =3D LLMRetryPolicy(
    llm_conn_id=3D"pydanticai_default",
    fallback_rules=3D[
        RetryRule(exception=3DConnectionError, action=3DRetryAction.RETRY, =
retry_delay=3Dtimedelta(seconds=3D10)),
        RetryRule(exception=3DPermissionError, action=3DRetryAction.FAIL),
    ],
)</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <h1 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-RelationshiptoOtherAIPs">Relati=
onship to <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"7673d77a-b60e-4=
3f5-a9c6-6beea09d68cf">Other AIPs</span></h1>
    <ul>
     <li><strong><a href=3D"/confluence/spaces/AIRFLOW/pages/311626182/AIP-=
72+Task+Execution+Interface+aka+Task+SDK">AIP-72 (Task SDK)</a></strong>: R=
etryPolicy is defined in the Task SDK and evaluated in the task runner proc=
ess, consistent with AIP-72's model of user code executing in workers.</li>
     <li><strong><a href=3D"/confluence/spaces/AIRFLOW/pages/406618285/AIP-=
99+Common+Data+Access+Pattern+AI">AIP-99 (AI Provider Integration)</a></str=
ong>: The Common AI provider ships an <code>LLMRetryPolicy</code> that uses=
 PydanticAIHook for LLM-based error classification. This is an optional enh=
ancement, not a core dependency.</li>
     <li><strong><a href=3D"/confluence/spaces/AIRFLOW/pages/406623137/AIP-=
103+Task+State+Management">AIP-103 (Task State Management)</a></strong>: Re=
tryDecision reasons could be exposed via Task State for observability, thou=
gh this is out of scope for the initial implementation.</li>
    </ul>
    <h1 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Considerations">Considerations<=
/h1>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Whatchangedoyoupropose?">What c=
hange do you propose?</h2>
    <p>Add a <code>retry_policy</code> parameter to <code>BaseOperator</cod=
e> that accepts a <code>RetryPolicy</code> object. The policy evaluates the=
 exception at failure time and returns a <code>RetryDecision</code> that ca=
n override the retry/fail decision and the retry delay. The existing flat p=
arameters (<code>retries</code>, <code>retry_delay</code>, <code>retry_expo=
nential_backoff</code>, <code>max_retry_delay</code>) remain unchanged and =
serve as defaults when no policy is configured or when the policy defers to=
 standard behavior.</p>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Coretypes">Core types</h2>
    <p>New module in the Task SDK: <code>airflow.sdk.definitions.<span clas=
s=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"bc5b0ddb-5318-4e9f-b04f-c90e861889f=
1">retry_policy</span></code></p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">class RetryAction(Enum):
    """What should happen after a failure."""
    RETRY =3D "retry"      # Retry the task
    FAIL =3D "fail"        # Fail immediately, skip remaining retries
    DEFAULT =3D "default"  # Fall through to standard retry logic


@dataclass(frozen=3DTrue)
class RetryDecision:
    """The result of evaluating a RetryPolicy."""
    action: RetryAction =3D RetryAction.DEFAULT
    retry_delay: timedelta | None =3D None   # Override delay; None =3D use=
 task's default
    reason: str | None =3D None              # Logged and stored for observ=
ability

    @classmethod
    def fail(cls, reason=3DNone) -&gt; RetryDecision:
        return cls(action=3DRetryAction.FAIL, reason=3Dreason)

    @classmethod
    def retry(cls, delay=3DNone, reason=3DNone) -&gt; RetryDecision:
        return cls(action=3DRetryAction.RETRY, retry_delay=3Ddelay, reason=
=3Dreason)

    @classmethod
    def default(cls) -&gt; RetryDecision:
        return cls(action=3DRetryAction.DEFAULT)


class RetryPolicy(abc.ABC):
    """
    Base class for retry policies.

    The evaluate() method runs in the task worker process and has full
    access to the exception object and the Airflow context.
    The scheduler never calls this.
    """

    @abc.abstractmethod
    def evaluate(
        self,
        exception: BaseException,
        try_number: int,
        max_tries: int,
        context: Context | None =3D None,
    ) -&gt; RetryDecision:
        """Evaluate whether and how to retry given the failure."""
        ...</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Declarativepolicyforcommoncases=
">Declarative policy for common cases</h2>
    <p><code>ExceptionRetryPolicy</code> maps exception types to retry beha=
viors without writing code:</p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">@dataclass
class RetryRule:
    """A single exception-to-behavior mapping."""
    exception: type[BaseException] | str | list  # Class, dotted path, or l=
ist of either
    action: RetryAction =3D RetryAction.RETRY
    retry_delay: timedelta | None =3D None
    reason: str | None =3D None
    match_subclasses: bool =3D True  # True =3D isinstance; False =3D exact=
 type


class ExceptionRetryPolicy(RetryPolicy):
    def __init__(self, rules: list[RetryRule], default: RetryAction =3D Ret=
ryAction.DEFAULT):
        self.rules =3D rules
        self.default =3D default

    def evaluate(self, exception, try_number, max_tries, context=3DNone) -&=
gt; RetryDecision:
        for rule in self.rules:
            if rule.matches(exception):
                return RetryDecision(
                    action=3Drule.action,
                    retry_delay=3Drule.retry_delay,
                    reason=3Drule.reason or f"Matched rule for {type(except=
ion).__name__}",
                )
        return RetryDecision(action=3Dself.default)</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <h3 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Exceptionstringvalidation">Exce=
ption string validation</h3>
    <p><code>RetryRule</code> validates exception strings at definition tim=
e:</p>
    <ul>
     <li>Strings without a dot (e.g., <code>"ValueError"</code> instead of =
<code>"builtins.ValueError"</code>) raise <code>ValueError</code> immediate=
ly, catching typos early.</li>
     <li>Dotted paths that can't be resolved at parse time <span class=3D"i=
nline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"4b79aca4-01eb-46b4-8262-ff8907c0a286">pro=
duce a warning</span> (they may resolve on the worker, which can have diffe=
rent packages installed).</li>
     <li>By default, rules use <code>isinstance</code> matching, so a rule =
for <code>OSError</code> also matches <code>ConnectionError</code> (a subcl=
ass). Set <code>match_subclasses=3DFalse</code> for exact type matching.</l=
i>
    </ul>
    <p>A rule can match multiple exception types at once:</p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false"># Multiple exceptions sharing the same behaviour
RetryRule(
    exception=3D[ConnectionError, TimeoutError, "requests.exceptions.HTTPEr=
ror"],
    action=3DRetryAction.RETRY,
    retry_delay=3Dtimedelta(seconds=3D30),
    reason=3D"Transient network error",
)</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-User-facingAPI">User-facing API=
</h2>
    <p>The <code>retry_policy</code> parameter works on any task or operato=
r:</p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">from airflow.sdk.definitions.retry_policy import=
 ExceptionRetryPolicy, RetryRule, RetryAction
from datetime import timedelta

@task(
    retries=3D5,
    retry_delay=3Dtimedelta(minutes=3D1),
    retry_policy=3DExceptionRetryPolicy(rules=3D[
        RetryRule(
            exception=3D"requests.exceptions.HTTPError",
            action=3DRetryAction.RETRY,
            retry_delay=3Dtimedelta(minutes=3D5),
            reason=3D"Likely rate limit, backing off",
        ),
        RetryRule(
            exception=3D"google.auth.exceptions.RefreshError",
            action=3DRetryAction.FAIL,
            reason=3D"Auth failure, not retryable",
        ),
        RetryRule(
            exception=3DConnectionError,
            action=3DRetryAction.RETRY,
            retry_delay=3Dtimedelta(seconds=3D30),
        ),
    ]),
)
def call_external_api():
    response =3D requests.get("https://api.example.com/data")
    response.raise_for_status()
    return response.json()</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <p>Works on operators, via <code>default_args</code>, and with mapped t=
asks:</p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false"># Operator
op =3D MyOperator(task_id=3D"x", retries=3D3, retry_policy=3Dmy_policy)

# Shared across a DAG via default_args
with DAG("dag", default_args=3D{"retry_policy": my_policy}):
    ...

# Mapped tasks -- policy applies per-instance
@task.partial(retry_policy=3Dmy_policy).expand(input=3D[1, 2, 3])
def my_mapped_task(input):
    ...</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Compositionwithexistingparamete=
rs">Composition with existing parameters</h2>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Existing param</th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Behavior when retry_policy is present</t=
h>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>retries</code></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Still the max retry count. <span class=
=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"0cd1ba8a-4f5a-4d49-8f91-1e47a7049698=
">Policy can fail earlier but not exceed this cap.</span></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>retry_delay</code> / <code>retry_e=
xponential_backoff</code> / <code>max_retry_delay</code></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Default delay calculation. Used when pol=
icy returns DEFAULT or <code>retry_delay=3DNone</code>.</td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>on_retry_callback</code></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Still <span class=3D"inline-comment-mark=
er" data-ref=3D"65d9fd9a-05bf-4640-86a9-5d795d9461a2">fires on all retries<=
/span>, including policy-driven retries.</td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><strong>Evaluation priority:</strong></p>
    <ol>
     <li><strong>AirflowFailException / AirflowSensorTimeout</strong>: Caug=
ht in a separate handler; policy never sees these. Explicit "do not retry" =
from task code always wins.</li>
     <li><strong>retry_policy.evaluate()</strong>: Runs for all other excep=
tions if a policy is configured. Can override to FAIL, <span class=3D"inlin=
e-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"cd5840e6-8ab9-457a-9411-d55ef55063c6">RETRY</=
span> with custom delay, or DEFAULT.</li>
     <li><strong>Standard retry logic</strong>: <code>should_retry</code> b=
ased on <code>try_number &lt;=3D max_tries</code>. Used when no policy is c=
onfigured or policy returns DEFAULT.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Executionflow">Execution flow</=
h2>
    <p>The <code>context</code> parameter passed to <code>evaluate()</code>=
 is the standard Airflow template context dict, including: <code>dag_run</c=
ode>, <code>params</code>, <code>task_instance</code>, <code>ds</code>, <co=
de>logical_date</code>, <code>var</code> (variables), <code>conn</code> (co=
nnections), and all other template reference fields.</p>
    <p>The policy evaluates in the <strong>task worker process</strong>, be=
tween catching the exception and communicating state to the API server. Eac=
h decision is logged in the task logs as <code>Retry policy decision action=
=3D&lt;action&gt; reason=3D&lt;reason&gt;</code>.</p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">def _evaluate_retry_policy(
    ti: RuntimeTaskInstance,
    exception: BaseException,
    log: Logger,
    context: Context | None =3D None,
) -&gt; RetryDecision | None:
    """Evaluate the task's retry policy. Returns None if no policy configur=
ed."""
    policy =3D getattr(ti.task, "retry_policy", None)
    if policy is None:
        return None
    try:
        decision =3D policy.evaluate(
            exception=3Dexception,
            try_number=3Dti.try_number,
            max_tries=3Dti._ti_context_from_server.max_tries,
            context=3Dcontext,
        )
        if decision.reason:
            log.info("Retry policy decision: %s (%s)", decision.action.valu=
e, decision.reason)
        return decision
    except Exception:
        log.exception("Retry policy evaluation failed, using default behavi=
or")
        return None</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Communicatingtheretrydelayoverr=
idetothescheduler">Communicating the retry delay override to the scheduler<=
/h2>
    <p>The policy runs in the worker. The retry delay is computed in the sc=
heduler via <code>next_retry_datetime()</code>. The override must cross the=
 process boundary.</p>
    <p><strong>Protocol change:</strong> Add <code>retry_delay_seconds</cod=
e> and <code>retry_reason</code> to <code>TIRetryStatePayload</code>:</p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">class TIRetryStatePayload(StrictBaseModel):
    state: Literal[IntermediateTIState.UP_FOR_RETRY]
    end_date: UtcDateTime
    rendered_map_index: str | None =3D None
    retry_delay_seconds: float | None =3D None   # NEW: policy-overridden d=
elay
    retry_reason: str | None =3D None            # NEW: human-readable reas=
on</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <p><strong>Data model change:</strong> Add two nullable columns to <cod=
e>TaskInstance</code>:</p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">retry_delay_override: Mapped[float | None] =3D m=
apped_column(Float, nullable=3DTrue)
retry_reason: Mapped[str | None] =3D mapped_column(String(500), nullable=3D=
True)</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <p><strong>Scheduler change:</strong> <code>next_retry_datetime()</code=
> checks the override first:</p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">def next_retry_datetime(self):
    if self.retry_delay_override is not None:
        return self.end_date + timedelta(seconds=3Dself.retry_delay_overrid=
e)
    # Existing exponential backoff calculation (unchanged)
    ...</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <p><strong>Execution API versioning:</strong> New version file with Cad=
wyn version change. Old workers that don't send the new fields omit them (d=
efaults to None). Old servers ignore them via Cadwyn stripping. Full backwa=
rd compatibility in both directions.</p>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-DAGserialization">DAG serializa=
tion</h2>
    <p>The serialized DAG stores a boolean flag <code>has_retry_policy</cod=
e> (matching the pattern used for callbacks like <code>has_on_retry_callbac=
k</code>). The full policy object is not serialized. The scheduler only nee=
ds to know whether a policy exists (for UI display); it never evaluates the=
 policy. The API server has no use for the policy object either. The worker=
 parses the DAG file directly and has the live policy object, which is wher=
e <code>evaluate()</code> runs.</p>
    <p>This means:</p>
    <ul>
     <li>No custom serialization/deserialization code for policy classes</l=
i>
     <li>No requirement for custom RetryPolicy subclasses to be importable =
on the API server</li>
     <li>Older Airflow versions that encounter <code>has_retry_policy</code=
> in a serialized DAG simply ignore it</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Securityconsiderations">Securit=
y considerations</h2>
    <ul>
     <li><strong>Exception content as LLM input:</strong> When using <code>=
LLMRetryPolicy</code>, exception messages are sent to the configured LLM. U=
sers handling sensitive data can use local models (Ollama/vLLM) so error lo=
gs never leave the infrastructure.</li>
     <li><strong>Policy execution scope:</strong> The policy runs in the sa=
me process as the task, with the same permissions. It cannot escalate privi=
leges.</li>
     <li><strong>Timeout protection:</strong> <code>LLMRetryPolicy</code> e=
nforces a configurable timeout (default 30 seconds) on LLM calls. If the pr=
ovider is degraded, the policy falls back to <code>fallback_rules</code> wi=
thin the timeout. Connection failures fall back in under 1 second.</li>
    </ul>
    <h1 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-IntegrationwithAIP-99(AIProvide=
rIntegration)">Integration with AIP-99 (AI Provider Integration)</h1>
    <p>The Common AI provider (<code>apache-airflow-providers-common-ai</co=
de>) ships an <code>LLMRetryPolicy</code> as an optional, higher-level poli=
cy built on the core <code>RetryPolicy</code> abstraction.</p>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-LLMRetryPolicy">LLMRetryPolicy<=
/h2>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">class ErrorClassification(BaseModel):
    """Structured LLM output for error classification."""
    category: str           # rate_limit, auth, network, data, transient, p=
ermanent
    should_retry: bool
    suggested_delay_seconds: int =3D 0
    reasoning: str


class LLMRetryPolicy(RetryPolicy):
    """
    Uses PydanticAIHook to call any LLM provider for error classification.
    Falls back to fallback_rules when LLM call fails.
    Enforces a configurable timeout (default 30s).
    """
    def __init__(self, llm_conn_id, model_id=3DNone, instructions=3DNone,
                 fallback_rules=3DNone, timeout=3D30.0):
        self.llm_conn_id =3D llm_conn_id
        self.model_id =3D model_id
        self.instructions =3D instructions or self._default_instructions()
        self.fallback_rules =3D fallback_rules
        self.timeout =3D timeout

    def evaluate(self, exception, try_number, max_tries, context=3DNone):
        try:
            return self._classify_with_timeout(exception, try_number, max_t=
ries)
        except Exception:
            if self.fallback_rules:
                return ExceptionRetryPolicy(rules=3Dself.fallback_rules).ev=
aluate(
                    exception, try_number, max_tries, context)
            return RetryDecision.default()

    def _classify_with_timeout(self, exception, try_number, max_tries):
        import concurrent.futures
        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=3D1) as exec=
utor:
            future =3D executor.submit(self._classify, exception, try_numbe=
r, max_tries)
            return future.result(timeout=3Dself.timeout)

    def _classify(self, exception, try_number, max_tries):
        from airflow.providers.common.ai.hooks.pydantic_ai import PydanticA=
IHook
        hook =3D PydanticAIHook(llm_conn_id=3Dself.llm_conn_id, model_id=3D=
self.model_id)
        agent =3D hook.create_agent(output_type=3DErrorClassification,
                                  instructions=3Dself.instructions)
        result =3D agent.run_sync(
            f"Classify this error (attempt {try_number}/{max_tries}):\n\n{e=
xception}")
        c =3D result.output
        if not c.should_retry:
            return RetryDecision.fail(reason=3Df"{c.category}: {c.reasoning=
}")
        delay =3D (timedelta(seconds=3Dc.suggested_delay_seconds)
                 if c.suggested_delay_seconds &gt; 0 else None)
        return RetryDecision.retry(delay=3Ddelay,
                                   reason=3Df"{c.category}: {c.reasoning}")=
</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <p><strong>Usage:</strong></p>
    <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
     <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
      <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D=
"brush: py; gutter: false">from airflow.providers.common.ai.policies.retry =
import LLMRetryPolicy

# Any LLM provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, Bedrock, Vertex, Ollama, etc.)
@task(retries=3D5, retry_policy=3DLLMRetryPolicy(llm_conn_id=3D"my_llm"))
def call_flaky_api(): ...

# Local-only (Ollama -- error logs never leave infrastructure)
@task(retries=3D3, retry_policy=3DLLMRetryPolicy(
    llm_conn_id=3D"ollama_local", model_id=3D"ollama:llama3.2"))
def sensitive_task(): ...

# LLM with declarative fallback
@task(retries=3D5, retry_policy=3DLLMRetryPolicy(
    llm_conn_id=3D"my_llm",
    timeout=3D15.0,
    fallback_rules=3D[
        RetryRule(exception=3DConnectionError, retry_delay=3Dtimedelta(seco=
nds=3D10)),
    ]))
def call_api(): ...</pre>
     </div>
    </div>
    <h1 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Whichusersareaffected?">Which u=
sers are affected?</h1>
    <p><strong>DAG authors:</strong> Gain a new optional parameter (<code>r=
etry_policy</code>) on all tasks and operators. No existing DAGs are affect=
ed.</p>
    <p><strong>Operator authors:</strong> No changes required. RetryPolicy =
is evaluated by the task runner, not by operators.</p>
    <p><strong>Platform operators:</strong> A database migration adds two n=
ullable columns (<code>retry_delay_override</code>, <code>retry_reason</cod=
e>) to the <code>task_instance</code> table. On PostgreSQL and MySQL 8+, nu=
llable columns with no defaults are metadata-only operations (no table rewr=
ite).</p>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Migrationeffort">Migration effo=
rt</h2>
    <p>None. The feature is entirely opt-in. Existing DAGs with <code>retri=
es</code> and <code>retry_delay</code> continue to work identically. The ne=
w columns have no effect on tasks without a <code>retry_policy</code>.</p>
    <h2 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Downsides">Downsides</h2>
    <ul>
     <li><strong>Additional latency on failure path:</strong> When using <c=
ode>LLMRetryPolicy</code>, the LLM call adds 1-3 seconds to the failure han=
dling path. This happens only on failures, not on the happy path. For the d=
eclarative <code>ExceptionRetryPolicy</code>, overhead is negligible.</li>
     <li><strong>LLM reliability:</strong> If the LLM call fails during ret=
ry evaluation, the policy falls back to <code>fallback_rules</code> or defa=
ult behavior within the configured timeout (default 30s). Connection failur=
es fall back in under 1 second.</li>
     <li><strong>New DB columns:</strong> Two nullable columns on <code>tas=
k_instance</code>. The <code>retry_reason</code> column (VARCHAR 500) adds =
minimal storage overhead.</li>
    </ul>
    <h1 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-Outofscope">Out of scope</h1>
    <ul>
     <li><strong>Retry budgets per DAG or DAG run.</strong> A system-level =
cap on total retries across all tasks in a DAG run is a separate feature.</=
li>
     <li><strong>Automatic retry policy suggestion.</strong> Analyzing hist=
orical failures to recommend policies could be a follow-up feature.</li>
     <li><strong>UI for configuring retry policies.</strong> Policies are d=
efined in code (DAG files), not via the UI.</li>
     <li><strong>Retry delay as a callable.</strong> Making <code>retry_del=
ay</code> accept a callable was considered but rejected in favor of the pol=
icy pattern, which is more composable.</li>
    </ul>
    <h1 id=3D"AIP105:PluggableRetryPolicies-WhatdefinesthisAIPas&quot;done&=
quot;?">What defines this AIP as "done"?</h1>
    <ol>
     <li><code>RetryPolicy</code>, <code>RetryDecision</code>, <code>RetryA=
ction</code>, <code>RetryRule</code>, and <code>ExceptionRetryPolicy</code>=
 classes available in <code>airflow.sdk.definitions.retry_policy</code>.</l=
i>
     <li><code>retry_policy</code> parameter accepted on <code>BaseOperator=
</code> and the <code>@task</code> decorator.</li>
     <li>Policy evaluation wired into <code>task_runner.py</code> exception=
 handling, with proper fallback on policy errors.</li>
     <li><code>TIRetryStatePayload</code> accepts <code>retry_delay_seconds=
</code> and <code>retry_reason</code>.</li>
     <li><code>TaskInstance</code> model has <code>retry_delay_override</co=
de> and <code>retry_reason</code> columns with corresponding migration.</li=
>
     <li><code>next_retry_datetime()</code> respects <code>retry_delay_over=
ride</code>.</li>
     <li>Execution API version change ensures backward compatibility with o=
lder workers/servers.</li>
     <li><code>has_retry_policy</code> boolean flag in serialized DAGs (mat=
ching the callback pattern).</li>
     <li><code>LLMRetryPolicy</code> ships in <code>apache-airflow-provider=
s-common-ai</code> with timeout and fallback support.</li>
     <li>Documentation covers the feature with examples for common use case=
s.</li>
     <li>Unit and integration tests cover: rule matching, policy evaluation=
 in task_runner, delay override in scheduler, LLM policy with fallback.</li=
>
    </ol>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
